"What are the potential causes and recommended solutions for the 'ORA-04031: unable to allocate shared memory' error that occurred twice within one minute on Linux platform for database instance PCNE00112? How can we prevent this issue from recurring in the future, and what steps should be taken to monitor and manage shared memory allocation more effectively?"
2025-03-13 15:43:05 | INFO | backend:_conversation:291 - 收到前端请求数据: {'query': 'Based on the provided text, which appears to be an Oracle Database alert log entry, here\'s a deep question:\n\n"What are the potential causes and recommended solutions for the \'ORA-04031: unable to allocate shared memory\' error that occurred twice within one minute on Linux platform for database instance PCNE00112? How can we prevent this issue from recurring in the future, and what steps should be taken to monitor and manage shared memory allocation more effectively?"', 'result': "The ORA-04031 error typically occurs when there is not enough shared memory available for Oracle Database to allocate. Here are some potential causes and recommended solutions for this issue:\n\n**Potential Causes:**\n\n1. **Insufficient Shared Memory**: The most common cause is that the shared memory allocated for Oracle Database is insufficient for its needs.\n2. **High System Load**: High system load due to other processes or activities can consume available memory, leaving none for Oracle Database.\n3. **Large Sort/Hash Operations**: Large sort or hash operations can temporarily require more shared memory than is available.\n4. **Insufficient Swap Space**: If the system runs out of physical memory, it uses swap space. However, swapping can cause performance degradation and may not be sufficient to handle large memory requirements.\n\n**Recommended Solutions:**\n\n1. **Check Shared Memory Configuration**: Ensure that the shared memory configuration (`SHARED_POOL_SIZE`, `LARGE_POOL_SIZE`, etc.) is appropriate for your workload. You might need to increase these settings based on your system's available memory.\n2. **Monitor System Load**: Keep an eye on system load using tools like `top` or `htop`. If the system load is consistently high, consider optimizing or reducing other processes running on the system.\n3. **Limit Large Sort/Hash Operations**: If possible, limit large sort or hash operations by using appropriate indexes or partitioning strategies to reduce the amount of data that needs to be sorted or hashed.\n4. **Increase Swap Space**: If your system is consistently swapping, consider increasing swap space. However, keep in mind that swapping can cause performance degradation.\n\n**Preventive Measures:**\n\n1. **Regularly Monitor Shared Memory Usage**: Use tools like `v$sgastat` and `v$sgastatmgr` to monitor shared memory usage and ensure that there is enough free memory available.\n2. **Set Alerts for Low Shared Memory**: Configure alerts to notify you when shared memory usage falls below a certain threshold, allowing you to take proactive measures before an ORA-04031 error occurs.\n\n**Steps to Monitor and Manage Shared Memory Allocation:**\n\n1. Regularly check `v$sgastat` and `v$sgastatmgr` views to monitor shared memory usage.\n2. Set alerts for low shared memory using Oracle's Enterprise Manager or by creating custom PL/SQL scripts.\n3. Periodically review and tune your shared memory configuration based on your workload and system resources.\n4. Monitor system load and swap space usage to ensure that other processes are not consuming excessive amounts of memory.\n5. Regularly analyze and optimize SQL queries to minimize large sort or hash operations.\n\nBy following these steps, you can effectively monitor and manage shared memory allocation, preventing ORA-04031 errors from recurring in the future.", 'source_documents': [Document(metadata={'source': '/root/mentor_agent/oradoc/故障应急预案_ORA-4031_v1.0.docx'}, page_content='ORA-4031应急预案\nORA-4031是Oracle数据库进程（前台进程或后台进程都有可能）向数据库实例的Shared Pool（或其他）申请一块共有内存时，数据库实例无法从持有的SGA中找到符合要求的内存时发生的错误。  \n数据库进程在发生ORA-4031时会中断。如果这个进程是前台进程，应用程序会接收到ORA-4031报错，应用程序需要进行回滚或其他方式的应用恢复。如果这个进程是后台进程，则有可能引起数据库实例重启等。'), Document(metadata={'source': '/root/mentor_agent/oradoc/故障应急预案_ORA-4031_v1.0.docx'}, page_content='ORA-4031应急预案-ORA-4031应急处理步骤\n检查SGA中各组件的状况  \n一般应急状况下，处理的第一时间不用去检查共享池碎片，意义不大。而且4031错误同样有可能导致整个数据库实例hang，所以应该去检查什么组件大小比较异常（有条件的话同类似的其他库环境去对比）。  \nselect t.* From (Select Name, round(bytes / (1024 * 1024),2) "MB",round(bytes / (Select sum(bytes) From v$sgainfo t  \nWhere t.name = \'Shared Pool Size\') * 100,2) || \'%\' "USED%" From v$sgastat Where pool = \'shared pool\' Order By 2 Desc) t Where rownum < 20;  \n可以回收空间的组件占比大  \n根据当前组件大小状态，判断是哪部分出了问题，如果是可以回收空间的组件，条件允许的话通过flush shared_pool来处理。比如sql area、Child cursor等占据主要大小，可能与硬解析有关，可以通过下面的查询确认：  \ncolumn FORCE_MATCHING_SIGNATURE format 99999999999999999999999  \nwith c as  \n(select force_matching_signature, count(*) cnt  \nfrom v$sqlarea  \nwhere force_matching_signature != 0  \ngroup by force_matching_signature  \nhaving count(*) > 20),  \nsq as  \n(select sql_text,  \nforce_matching_signature,  \nrow_number() over(partition by force_matching_signature order by sql_id desc) p  \nfrom v$sqlarea s  \nwhere force_matching_signature in  \n(select force_matching_signature from c))  \nselect sq.sql_text, sq.force_matching_signature, c.cnt "unshared count"  \nfrom c, sq  \nwhere sq.force_matching_signature = c.force_matching_signature  \nand sq.p = 1  \norder by c.cnt desc;  \nNote:  \nflush shared_pool 可能引起“解析风暴”导致CPU使用率激增，需要充分评估后执行。  \n无法回收的组件占比大  \n如果是无法回收的perm组件，则必须重启实例。  \n如果情况特别紧急，可以考虑临时缩小Buffer cache，调大shared pool，等到维护窗口后再重启实例恢复。  \n--确认现在SGA使用状况  \nSelect nvl(pool,name) "pool", Sum(bytes) / (1024 * 1024) "MB"  \nFrom v$sgastat  \nGroup By nvl(pool,name)  \norder by Sum(bytes) / (1024 * 1024) desc;  \npool MB  \n-------------------------- ----------  \nbuffer_cache 1104  \nshared pool 336  \nlarge pool 32  \njava pool 16  \nlog_buffer 7.125  \nfixed_sga 2.14918518  \n6 rows selected.  \nSQL> SHOW PARAMETER shared_pool_size  \nNAME TYPE VALUE  \n------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------  \nshared_pool_size big integer 0  \nSQL> SHOW PARAMETER db_cache_size  \nNAME TYPE VALUE  \n------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------  \ndb_cache_size big integer 0  \n--确认Granule Size  \nselect bytes/(1024 * 1024) " Granule Size (MB)" from v$sgainfo where name like \'Granule Size\';  \nGranule Size (MB)  \n------------------  \n16  \n--缩小db_cache_size – 80M  \nalter system set db_cache_size = 1024M scope=memory;  \n--增大shared_pool_size + 80M  \nalter system set shared_pool_size = 416M scope=memory;  \nSystem altered.  \nSQL> SHOW PARAMETER shared_pool_size  \nNAME TYPE VALUE  \n------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------  \nshared_pool_size big integer 416M  \nSQL> SHOW PARAMETER db_cache_size  \nNAME TYPE VALUE  \n------------------------------------ ----------- ------------------------------  \ndb_cache_size big integer 1G  \nSQL> Select nvl(pool,name) "pool", Sum(bytes) / (1024 * 1024) "MB"  \nFrom v$sgastat  \nGroup By nvl(pool,name)  \norder by Sum(bytes) / (1024 * 1024) desc;  \npool MB  \n-------------------------- ----------  \nbuffer_cache 1024  \nshared pool 416  \nlarge pool 32  \njava pool 16  \nlog_buffer 7.125  \nfixed_sga 2.14918518  \n6 rows selected.  \nNote:  \n1. 上述命令会把 Buffer Cache 中的部分数据块 purge 出 SGA，从而引起物理I/O增多，需要充分评估后执行。\n2. 上述调整的大小必须是最小单位是“Granule unit”大小的整数倍。\n3. 上述命令可能因为其他关联参数（sga_target/ sga_max_size、memory_target/ memory_max_target等）设置和SGA的使用状况失败。'), Document(metadata={'source': '/root/mentor_agent/oradoc/故障应急预案_ORA-4031_v1.0.docx'}, page_content='ORA-4031 信息采集和后续分析\n在重启或者刷新shared_pool前，收集相关信息留做进一步的根因诊断。  \n* ORA-4031 诊断数据1  \nconn / as sysdba  \n@srdc_db_ora4031.sql  \n* ORA-4031 诊断数据2  \n例子：  \ntfactl diagcollect –srdc ORA-04031  \ntfactl diagcollect –srdc ORA-04031 -database db -from "Mar/13/2015" -to "Mar/13/2015 15:00:00"  \n* ash dump 数据  \nconn / as sysdba  \n@ash_dump.sql  \n* awr Report 数据  \nconn / as sysdba  \n@awr_report.sql  \n* dba_hist_sgastat 数据  \nconn / as sysdba  \nset lines 300 pages 9999  \ncol name format a40  \ncol begin_interval_time format a30  \nPrompt \'Large memory allocation component\'  \nselect a.instance_number,b.begin_interval_time,a.name,a.pool,a.bytes  \nfrom dba_hist_sgastat a, dba_hist_snapshot b  \nwhere a.snap_id=b.snap_id  \nand a.instance_number = b.instance_number  \nand a.dbid = b.dbid  \nand a.bytes >= 200*1024*1024  \nand begin_interval_time>= sysdate - 14  \norder by a.instance_number,b.begin_interval_time,a.bytes;  \n* OSW 数据  \ncd oswbb/archive  \nfind . -name "*22.03.18.2[1-3]*" -exec zip /tmp/osw_`hostname`_220317_21-23.zip {} \\;  \n* TFA 数据  \nsu - root  \ntfactl diagcollect -from "Jun/12/2022 18:00:00" -to "Jun/21/2022 23:59:59"  \n* OPATCH 数据  \nopatch lsinventory -detail'), Document(metadata={'source': '/root/mentor_agent/oradoc/statistics.md'}, page_content='如何诊断表统计信息是否过期流程\n\n获取 PLAN 包含表的统计信息情况\n\n这是整个流程的起点，表示从 PLAN 中获取表的统计信息。\n\n判断统计信息是否过期或被 restore\n\n如果统计信息未过期（否），则直接进入“统计信息正常”状态。\n\n如果统计信息过期或被 restore，则需要进一步检查。\n\n判断是否为大表或大分区过期\n\n如果是大表或大分区过期（是），则需要进一步检查。\n\n如果不是大表或大分区过期（否），则继续进行常规的统计信息检查。\n\n判断数据变化率是否大于阈值\n\n如果数据变化率大于阈值（是），则需要处理统计信息过期，变化率大的情况。\n\n如果数据变化率不大于阈值（否），则统计信息过期但变化率不大，直接进入“Pass End”。\n\n检查特定日志文件\n\n对于大表或大分区统计信息过期且变化率大的情况，需要检查 check_result.log。\n\n对于统计信息过期但变化率不大的情况，需要检查 check_result.log。\n\n检查参数日志\n\n针对统计信息过期的表，需要检查 check_param.log。\n\n收集统计信息\n\n在检查日志后，需要执行“Gather Stats”操作，以更新统计信息。\n\n结束流程\n\n经过以上步骤后，如果一切正常，则流程结束，标记为“Pass End”。')]}
